{
  "key": "firefly",
  "meta": {
    "label": "Firefly Sync",
    "group": "organic",
    "thumbnail": "bi-lightning-charge"
  },
  "intro": {
    "summary": "Oscillator coupling and flash synchronization",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Independent rhythms can suddenly lock together when nearby oscillators influence each other.",
      "Coupling strength, interaction radius, frequency jitter, and phase noise guide phase locking, until many small clocks begin to breathe in the same light."
    ]
  },
  "model": {
    "references": [
      {
        "label": "Wikipedia: Kuramoto model",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuramoto_model"
      },
      {
        "label": "Wikipedia: Synchronization",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synchronization"
      }
    ],
    "journalArticles": [
      {
        "title": "Synchronization of Pulse-Coupled Biological Oscillators",
        "url": "https://doi.org/10.1137/0150098"
      }
    ],
    "items": [
      {
        "title": "Phase (\\(\\theta\\))",
        "equation": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\mathcal{N}_i&=\\left\\{j\\neq i:\\left\\lVert\\mathbf{x}_j-\\mathbf{x}_i\\right\\rVert\\le r\\right\\}\\\\\\theta_i(t+\\Delta t)&=\\theta_i(t)+\\left(\\omega_i + \\frac{K}{N_i}\\sum_{j\\in\\mathcal{N}_i}\\sin(\\theta_j-\\theta_i) + \\eta_i(t)\\right)\\Delta t\\end{aligned}$$",
        "explanation": "Each firefly advances according to its natural rhythm, coupling to neighbors, and a noise term.",
        "parameters": [
          "<strong>Coupling</strong> (\\(K\\)) sets the synchronization strength.",
          "<strong>Interaction Radius</strong> (\\(r\\)) defines which neighbors enter \\(\\mathcal{N}_i\\) for local coupling.",
          "<strong>Base Frequency</strong> (\\(\\omega\\)) sets the central intrinsic oscillation rate.",
          "<strong>Frequency Jitter</strong> (\\(\\Delta\\omega\\)) sets the oscillator-to-oscillator spread around the base rate.",
          "<strong>Phase Noise</strong> (\\(\\eta\\)) adds stochastic perturbations to phase evolution."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Blink Event",
        "equation": "$$\\theta_i \\mapsto \\theta_i \\bmod 2\\pi,\\quad \\text{blink when } \\theta_i \\to 2\\pi$$",
        "explanation": "A blink occurs when the phase completes a full cycle, after which the oscillator wraps back to the start of the next cycle."
      },
      {
        "title": "Synchronization Order (\\(R\\))",
        "equation": "$$R=\\left|\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{k=1}^N e^{\\,i\\theta_k}\\right|$$",
        "explanation": "The order parameter measures how tightly the fireflies align in phase, from incoherent flashing near zero to near-perfect synchrony near one."
      },
      {
        "title": "Initialization",
        "equation": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{x}_i(0)&\\sim \\mathcal{U}\\!\\left([-0.45L_x,0.45L_x]\\times[-0.45L_y,0.45L_y]\\times[-0.45L_z,0.45L_z]\\right)\\\\\\theta_i(0)&\\sim \\mathcal{U}(0,2\\pi)\\\\\\omega_i&\\sim \\mathcal{U}(\\omega-\\Delta\\omega,\\,\\omega+\\Delta\\omega)\\\\\\mathbf{v}_i(0)&=s\\,\\hat{\\mathbf{u}}_i,\\ \\lVert\\hat{\\mathbf{u}}_i\\rVert=1\\end{aligned}$$",
        "explanation": "Fireflies begin from a uniform random spatial cloud with uniformly random initial phase, while intrinsic frequencies are drawn around the base rate using jitter. Initial speed magnitude is constant at the configured speed, with only direction randomized. Motion speed is not initialization-only: the same speed parameter also sets the runtime target magnitude of random-walk velocity during stepping.",
        "parameters": [
          "<strong>World Sizes</strong> (\\(L_x,L_y,L_z\\)) set the spawn volume extent.",
          "<strong>Base Frequency</strong> (\\(\\omega\\)) and <strong>Frequency Jitter</strong> (\\(\\Delta\\omega\\)) define the intrinsic frequency ensemble.",
          "<strong>Speed</strong> (\\(s\\)) sets both initial velocity magnitude and ongoing random-walk velocity scale."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
